How to Install the driver
1. login as root
2. Go to the directory which contains the souce
3. make
4. make install

How to use the driver
When you plug in the Spreadtrum's devices after the driver has been installed, you can find two tty devices which are named sprd_usb_modem0
and sprd_usb_diag1 in /dev directory. You can use /dev/sprd_usb_modem0 as a usb modem to connect to the network.

How to Uninstall the driver
1. login as root
2. Go to the directory which contains the souce
3. make uninstall

Note
1. The driver depends on the usb-serial module of linux kernel, make sure your system has this module compiled and load usb-serial module before load the sciu2s.ko. If your udev works correcly, both usb-serial and sciu2s module will be loaded automatically.
2. If you can not find /dev/sprd_usb_*** after plug in Spreadtrum's devices, try to find /dev/ttyUSB* devices. This may happen in some systems with udev of old versions.
